Subject: squashfs: add genfscon alongside fs_use_xattr

squashfs is a read-only filesystem that does not support security
xattrs.  The existing fs_use_xattr entry never matches at mount time;
the kernel falls back to unlabeled_t for all squashfs content.

Add a dedicated squashfs_t with genfscon so the kernel assigns a
known type.  The fs_use_xattr line is retained for completeness
(if a future squashfs implementation adds xattr support, it will
take precedence per the kernel's fs_use > genfscon priority).

Pattern follows virtiofs_t.

Upstream-Status: Pending [https://github.com/SELinuxProject/refpolicy/pull/1181]
---
--- a/policy/modules/kernel/filesystem.te
+++ b/policy/modules/kernel/filesystem.te
@@ -191,6 +191,15 @@
 fs_type(spufs_t)
 genfscon spufs / gen_context(system_u:object_r:spufs_t,s0)
 files_mountpoint(spufs_t)
+#
+# squashfs_t is the type for squashfs file systems.
+# squashfs is read-only and does not support xattrs;
+# the fs_use_xattr entry above never matches.
+#
+type squashfs_t;
+fs_noxattr_type(squashfs_t)
+files_mountpoint(squashfs_t)
+genfscon squashfs / gen_context(system_u:object_r:squashfs_t,s0)
 type sysv_t;
 fs_noxattr_type(sysv_t)
